{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.LadderPhaseFromWeights","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.LadderPhaseFromWeights","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.LadderPhaseMirrorCovariance"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zD_loopMean_num","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zD_loopMean_num","kind":"theorem","line":315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseFromWeights.lean#L315-L320","doc":"The same, denominator-cleared: `(2·z_D - h)·q·(q²+1) = q⁴ + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zD_loopMean_eq_twoQ_mul_xi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zD_loopMean_eq_twoQ_mul_xi","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseFromWeights.lean#L299-L313","doc":"**The D-frame loop mean, in closed form.**\n\n`2·z_D - h = [2]_q · (q⁴+1)/(q²+1)²`, i.e. the moment `Ξ` of §2 takes the\nvalue `(1+Q²)/(1+Q)²` with `Q = q²` — for every `n`, by\n`moment_independent_of_index`. Stated denominator-cleared so it is a\npolynomial identity.\n\nAt `n = 3` this value coincides with the single weight `y_(3)`, because\n`χ^(2,1)(τ) = 0`, `y_(1³) = 0` and `[4]_Q = (1+Q)(1+Q²)`. That coincidence\nis special to `n = 3` and should not be read as `Ξ = y_(n)` in general. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.zD_loopMean_sub_two_num","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.zD_loopMean_sub_two_num","kind":"theorem","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseFromWeights.lean#L287-L297","doc":"**`2·z_D - h - 2` has numerator `q⁴ - 2q³ - 2q + 1`.**\n\n`2q³/(q²+1) - (q - q⁻¹) - 2 = (q⁴ - 2q³ - 2q + 1)/(q(q²+1))`, so the\n`§3` hypothesis `2z - h ≠ 2` is exactly the non-vanishing of that quartic.\nStated denominator-cleared. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.no_weight_function_gives_phase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.no_weight_function_gives_phase","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseFromWeights.lean#L241-L278","doc":"**No function of the weight vector reproduces the ladder phase.**\n\nThe hypotheses are the real ones and none is decorative:\n* `hbar : zb = z - h` — how bar acts on the Markov parameter under D\n  (`zD_bar_eq_negative_loop`: bar exchanges the two stabilisation loop\n  values);\n* `hy : ybar = y` — the weight vector is bar-EVEN. Proved for the D-frame\n  weights as `markovWeightsD_y21_barEven` / `markovWeightsD_y3_barEven`,\n  hence so is any `F` of them;\n* `hF`, `hFbar` — the supposed function `F` reproduces the phase at `q`\n  and, because its argument is bar-fixed, returns the SAME value at `q⁻¹`;\n* `hh : h ≠ 0`, `hne : 2z - h ≠ 2` — non-degeneracy.\n\nThe conclusion is `False`: no such `G` exists.\n\n**Honesty about what `G` and `Y` contribute: nothing logical.** Once `hy`\nis substituted, `hF` and `hFbar` say only that the phase equals its own\nbar image, and the contradiction is `phaseTwice_not_bar_fixed` above.\n`G` and `Y` are carried because they are what makes the statement *read*\nas the exclusion it is — \"some function of the weight vector returns the\nphase\" — and because the bar-evenness of the weights is what supplies\n`hFbar` in any real application. The mathematics is entirely in the core\nlemma; this is its interpretation, not additional strength.\n\nNote what this does and does not exclude. It excludes the weights *alone*\ndetermining `alpha`; it does not touch §2, where `alpha` is recovered from\nthe weights **together with `h`**. The two are consistent precisely\nbecause `h` is exactly the bar-odd datum the weights cannot see — `h`\ndistinguishes `q` from `q⁻¹`, and the weights do not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.phaseTwice_not_bar_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.phaseTwice_not_bar_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseFromWeights.lean#L218-L239","doc":"**The core clash: the phase is not bar-fixed.**\n\nUnder D bar sends `z ↦ z - h` (`zD_bar_eq_negative_loop`: it exchanges the\ntwo stabilisation loop values), so `phaseTwice (z-h) (-h)` is the phase's\nbar image. It equals the phase itself only when `h*(2z - h - 2) = 0`.\n\nThis is the whole mathematical content of the exclusion below; the wrapper\nthat follows adds only the reading. Note it is a genuine restriction:\nwithout `hne` the two sides DO coincide, so the hypothesis is not\ndecorative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.phaseTwice_eq_moment_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.phaseTwice_eq_moment_form","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseFromWeights.lean#L195-L211","doc":"**The phase in moment form: `4α = [2]_q·Ξ·h + h² - 2h`.**\n\nWritten on the doubled phase, `2·phaseTwice z h - h² = ([2]_q·Ξ - 2)·h`,\nwhich is `phaseTwice_projected_eq_loopMean` with the loop mean rewritten\nby §2. Equivalently `α = (h/4)·([2]_q·Ξ + h - 2)`.\n\nThe bar-odd content sits entirely in the outer `h`; `[2]_q` and `Ξ` are\nboth bar-even, so this exhibits the phase as `h × (bar-even, and pinned by\nthe weights)` — the shape `MarkovWeightsConventionD` predicted without\npinning. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.moment_independent_of_index","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.moment_independent_of_index","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseFromWeights.lean#L180-L193","doc":"**The transposition moment does not depend on `n`.**\n\n`2z - h` mentions no index set, so if two different `n` both satisfy §2\nagainst the same `q` and `z`, their moments agree. The `n`-independence of\n`Ξ` is therefore *forced* by the loop-mean identity rather than observed\nacross a table — the probe's n = 2..9 sweep confirms the premise but is\nnot what establishes the conclusion.\n\n(Only `[2]_q ≠ 0` is needed, i.e. `q² + 1 ≠ 0`; over `ℝ` that is\nautomatic.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.loopMean_eq_twoQ_mul_moment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.loopMean_eq_twoQ_mul_moment","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseFromWeights.lean#L146-L178","doc":"**`2z - h = [2]_q · Ξ`**, where `Ξ = Σ_λ χ^λ(τ)·y_λ`.\n\nHypotheses are exactly the two Markov conditions the weight vector is\n*defined* by — the normalisation `Σ f^λ y_λ = 1` and the stabilisation\n`Σ χ_λ(σ₁) y_λ = z` — plus the per-block eigenvalue decomposition, which\nis §1's input. No convention is fixed: `z` is arbitrary, so this holds in\nC, in D, and in any other frame.\n\nStated over an arbitrary `Finset ι` so it covers every `n` at once; the\ncaller supplies `mp`/`mm` as the two `σ₁`-eigenvalue multiplicities and\nthe conclusion's moment is `Σ (mp - mm)·y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.chi_sigma_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.chi_sigma_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseFromWeights.lean#L125-L142","doc":"**`2·χ_λ(σ₁) - h·f^λ = [2]_q·(mp - mm)`.**\n\nWith `χ_λ(σ₁) = q·mp - q⁻¹·mm` and `f^λ = mp + mm`, the `h = q - q⁻¹`\nmultiplying the dimension exactly cancels the bar-odd half of the\ncharacter, leaving the bar-EVEN `[2]_q` against the eigenvalue-multiplicity\n*difference*. That difference is the ordinary symmetric-group character\n`χ^λ(τ)` at a transposition — it is the `q → 1` value of `χ_λ(σ₁)`, where\n`σ₁ ↦ τ`, `q ↦ 1` and `-q⁻¹ ↦ -1`.\n\nThis one identity is the reason a bar-even weight vector can nonetheless\npin the bar-odd phase: the phase's `h` is not supplied by the weights, and\neverything the weights DO supply enters through `[2]_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.twoQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.twoQ","kind":"def","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/LadderPhaseFromWeights.lean#L122-L123","doc":"The quantum integer `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`. Bar-EVEN, unlike `h = q - q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}